Fix fatal error: PermissionsTest::createContentType() incompatible with core

Drupal\Tests\node\Traits\ContentTypeCreationTrait::createContentType()
gained a second parameter, bool $create_body = TRUE. The
metatag_extended_perms submodule's bundled functional test overrides
this method without the new parameter, which is a fatal
"Declaration ... must be compatible with ..." error thrown during
PHPUnit's test-suite discovery (parsing every test class to read its
@group annotations before any --group filtering happens), breaking
the entire test run.

Adding the missing parameter and passing it through to the parent call
is a pure signature fix with no behavior change (this override already
ignores the incoming $values and hardcodes ['type' => 'page']).

--- a/metatag_extended_perms/tests/src/Functional/PermissionsTest.php
+++ b/metatag_extended_perms/tests/src/Functional/PermissionsTest.php
@@ -193,8 +193,8 @@ class PermissionsTest extends BrowserTestBase {
   /**
    * {@inheritdoc}
    */
-  protected function createContentType(array $values = []): NodeType {
-    $type = parent::createContentType(['type' => 'page']);
+  protected function createContentType(array $values = [], bool $create_body = TRUE): NodeType {
+    $type = parent::createContentType(['type' => 'page'], $create_body);

     // Load a node form.
     $this->drupalGet('node/add/page');
